wireview-hwmon (1.4.0~24.04.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * LAN fleet monitoring: opt-in HTTP /sensors publisher (remote_enabled in
    /etc/wireview/config) so other instances can read this host's device.
  * Authenticated remote writes: POST /command signed with HMAC-SHA256 (shared
    secret), including remote device config read/write.
  * wireviewctl top: live terminal fleet monitor of local + remote devices.
  * Daily-rotating audit log in /var/log/wireview (log_days retention).
  * Configurable listener port (port=); publish fan duty and firmware build
    string in /sensors.
  * Ship a reference /etc/wireview/config documenting the defaults.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

wireview-hwmon (1.3.2~26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (Resolute Raccoon).
  * Fix build on kernels < 6.11: platform_driver::remove() returns int there
    and void from 6.11 onwards (e.g. RHEL 9 / 5.14-based kernels). Closes #1.

